<title>USA: U.S. brass mill copper stocks higher in Nov - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. brass mill copper stocks higher in Nov - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. brass mill copper stocks rose to 144,100 short tons (copper content) at the end of November from 141,900 short tons in October, American Bureau of Metal Statistics said.</p>
<p>Scrap consumption was 54,200 short tons in the month, down from an October tally of 37,500 short tons.</p>
<p>Refinery shapes consumption was 40,400 tons in November against 39,900 the previous month. Total brass mill shipments fell to 98,300 short tons from 104,200 in October. Total receipts were 100,500 short tons in November, down from October's 103,100 short tons.</p>
<p>--New York Commodities Desk 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
